\ ==== callers ( xt -- arr ) ====

\ The names of the colon definitions whose compiled bodies reference a word, as
\ strings in definition order.

: sq dup * ;
: direct 3 sq 1+ ;
: tail 4 sq ;
: quoted [ 1 2 ] [: sq :] map drop ;
: ticked ' sq execute ;
: unrelated 1 2 + ;
variable counter
: reads-counter counter ;
: writes-counter | ^counter | 5 to counter ;
: recursive dup 0 > if 1- recursive then ;

\ -- a call, a tail call, a call inside a quotation, and a ' literal all count
' sq callers . cr                                 \ [ "direct" "tail" "quoted" "ticked" ]

\ -- a primitive: the session's own callers among the many
' 1+ callers [: "direct" = :] filter . cr         \ [ "direct" ]

\ -- a variable: its readers and its writers
' counter callers . cr                            \ [ "reads-counter" "writes-counter" ]

\ -- recursion lists the word itself; a word nobody calls answers an empty array
' recursive callers . cr                          \ [ "recursive" ]
' unrelated callers . cr                          \ [ ]

\ -- a top-level quotation mentioning a word is not a definition, so it never appears
[: sq :] drop
' sq callers size . cr                            \ 4

\ -- error cases (grouped): a quotation, a curried token
[: 1 :] ' callers catch drop :message @ . cr      \ (expected a named word; got a quotation)
1 ' sq curry ' callers catch drop :message @ . cr \ (expected a named word; got a curried token)
